invariant: INV-14
file: cpu_cfg.h
catches: quic_loop_host
reason: cpu_cfg.h gives each architecture the other's bits: an arm64
  object takes CH_CPU_AVX2 and CH_CPU_VAES, which it has no path for, and
  an x86-64 object refuses them. test/test_cpu.h states each
  architecture's bits apart from CH_CPU_DEFINED, so test/quic_loop_cpu.h
  sees a refused bit taken on arm64 and a defined one refused on x86-64.

--- old
#ifdef __x86_64__
#define CH_CPU_DEFINED                                                                             \
--- new
#ifdef __aarch64__
#define CH_CPU_DEFINED                                                                             \
